  "number": 76,
  "shortId": "6JDGF",
  "priority": 16,
  "slug": "viewnode-choice-choice-primitive-compose-the-remaining-widgets-full-viewnode-coverage",
  "title": "viewnode-choice: Choice primitive + compose the remaining widgets (full ViewNode coverage)",
  "discussedAt": "",
  "contextReady": false,
  "contextReadyReason": "",
  "summary": "One value-carrying, content-composable Choice primitive; refactor Select/Tabs onto it; then realize arms for every remaining WidgetKind (ItemGroup, MarkerGroup, Grid, DockFrame, Toast) — closing ViewNode coverage.",
  "description": "Close **ViewNode coverage for the whole widget vocabulary**, on the model the user chose (2026-07-13): an option is **a node with a value and arbitrary content**, and options are **children** — not a `props[\"options\"]` list of strings.\n\n## Why this phase exists (supersedes `viewnode-task-1`)\n`viewnode-task-1` (\"complete realize coverage\") assumed the 8 missing kinds only needed *structured props*. Investigation showed they split into three different gaps, and the option-shaped ones need a **widget refactor**, not a prop:\n- `Select` (`heca-grid-ui/src/widgets/select.rs:77`) is **self-contained**: `new(options: Vec<String>)`, paints its dropdown rows itself and hit-tests them by arithmetic — no child components.\n- `Tabs` (`widgets/tabs.rs:51`) likewise \"lays its own segments from monospace metrics (no child components)\".\nBoth **hand-draw their content**, so both are refactor targets under the standing rule (AGENTS.md ⭐ WIDGET ARCHITECTURE: a widget's content is composed from child `Component`s, never hand-drawn). Exactly the `Button` refactor (`07d4c1a`, PR #237), twice.\n\n## The model (LOCKED with the user)\n```\nViewNode::new(WidgetKind::Select)\n    .prop(\"selected\", PropValue::Int(1))\n    .on(\"change\", Intent::new(\"set_level\"))\n    .child(ViewNode::new(WidgetKind::Choice).prop(\"value\", PropValue::Text(\"low\".into()))\n        .child(ViewNode::new(WidgetKind::Row)\n            .child(ViewNode::new(WidgetKind::Icon).prop(\"icon\", PropValue::Glyph(\"circle\".into())))\n            .child(ViewNode::new(WidgetKind::Label).text(\"LOW\"))))\n```\n- **`Choice`** = a selectable, **value-carrying** container whose content is **arbitrary children** (like `<option value=…>` / SwiftUI `.tag()`). Named `Choice` because a widget named `Option` would shadow `std::Option` at every call site.\n- **`Choice` and `Item` COEXIST** (user decision): `Item` is a *row layout* (leading / label / trailing); `Choice` is *any content + a value*. Both must be documented so the difference is unmistakable — including when to use which.\n- One option primitive, four consumers: `Select`, `Tabs`, and later `ContextMenu` / `CommandPalette`.\n- **Values flow into the intent**: the widgets keep tracking a selected **index** internally; `realize` captures each `Choice`'s `value` prop and dispatches the `change` intent with `args[\"value\"]`, so a plugin receives `{\"value\":\"high\"}` rather than an opaque index.\n- After this, **`PropValue::List` is needed only by `Grid`** (`areas` = list of strings, tracks = list) — it shrinks from \"the core mechanism\" to a `Grid` detail.\n\n## Decisions already taken\n- `ScrollBar` is **host-only, not plugin-authorable**: its state is live host signals (`content_extent` / `viewport_extent` / `offset`) that static, serializable data fundamentally cannot drive. A plugin uses `Scroll` (a `ScrollRegion`), never a raw scrollbar. To be *documented as such*, not realized.\n- Grid tracks are **CSS-like strings** parsed by `realize` (`\"1fr\"` → `Track::Fr(1.0)`, `\"22px\"` → `Track::Px`, `\"auto\"`/`\"min\"`/`\"max\"`); unknown tokens degrade to `Auto` (realize stays total for untrusted input). No new schema invented.\n- Named child slots (`DockFrame`'s `header` vs body; `Item`'s leading/trailing) via a **`slot` prop on the child node** — no change to the `ViewNode` shape, and it generalizes.\n\n## Files\n`heca-grid-ui/src/widgets/{choice.rs (new), select.rs, tabs.rs, item.rs, item_group.rs, dock_frame.rs, marker_group.rs, grid.rs, toast.rs, mod.rs}`, `heca-grid-ui/src/lib.rs` (exports), `heca/src/chrome/{view.rs, realize.rs}`, `heca-renderer/examples/showcase.rs`, `docs/widgets.md`, `AGENTS.md` if a rule changes.\n\n## Behaviors to preserve\nEvery existing call site of `Select`/`Tabs` keeps compiling (string-list constructors stay as **sugar that builds `Choice` children**, exactly like `Button::new(label)` does). Selection/keyboard/overlay semantics unchanged: `Select`'s `overlay_active` contract, flip/cap against the viewport, wheel + `MenuUp`/`MenuDown`/`Activate`/`Dismiss` intents; `Tabs`' animated sliding underline and `ItemPrevious`/`ItemNext`. Styling stays theme-driven; content color inherited via `PaintCx::with_content_color`; a control stays ONE Tab stop (`Base.focus_barrier`).\n\n## Gates (every task)\n`cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features` 0 warnings; `cargo test -p heca-grid-ui -p heca`; showcase green; do NOT run `cargo fmt`; rust SKILL review before commit; no commit until the user has tested. Docs per AGENTS.md: EXHAUSTIVE, with runnable examples for BOTH audiences (native builder + declarative `ViewNode`).",
